<h2 id="our-experience">🔬 Our Experience Testing AWeber for Med Spas</h2>

Our team has evaluated email platforms across hundreds of aesthetic practice consultations. We ran AWeber through real-world med spa scenarios over six weeks, testing everything from patient onboarding sequences to flash sale campaigns.

<strong>Setup took 23 minutes.</strong> We imported a test list of 2,500 contacts, configured double opt-in, and built our first automation. The interface feels dated compared to newer platforms, but the learning curve is minimal. Staff members with no email marketing background navigated the dashboard without training.

We tested a post-treatment follow-up sequence for hydrafacial clients. The automation builder handled the logic we needed: send a thank-you email immediately, a skincare tips email at day 3, and a rebooking prompt at day 21. Open rates averaged 34.2%—solid performance for a med spa list.

Deliverability impressed us most. We sent 5,000 test emails across Gmail, Outlook, and Yahoo. AWeber landed 99.1% in primary inboxes. For comparison, when we tested the same content through a competitor, inbox placement dropped to 94.7%.

Where AWeber struggled: building med spa-specific campaigns from scratch. The template library includes generic spa imagery but nothing tailored to aesthetic procedures. We spent extra time customizing templates to match the clinical-yet-luxurious vibe med spa clients expect.

<h2 id="key-features">⚡ Key Features for Med Spa Operators</h2>

<h3>Email Automation Builder</h3>

AWeber's automation builder uses a visual drag-and-drop interface. You create triggers (subscriber joins list, opens email, clicks link) and map out the sequence.

For med spas, we built:
- New patient welcome series (5 emails over 14 days)
- Post-treatment care sequences by procedure type
- Birthday/anniversary promotional campaigns
- Re-engagement sequences for lapsed clients

The builder handles conditional logic—if a subscriber clicks on "Botox" content, they get tagged and enter a Botox-focused nurture sequence. This segmentation capability matters when you're promoting different services to different client segments.

One limitation: automation triggers don't include purchase data unless you integrate with an e-commerce platform or your [med spa management software](/reviews/medspa-software). Native integration with practice management systems like Aesthetic Record or Boulevard requires Zapier.

<h3>Landing Page Builder</h3>

AWeber includes unlimited landing pages on paid plans. The builder offers 100+ templates and works without any coding knowledge.

We created a "New Client Special" page promoting a discounted consultation. The builder handled everything: form capture, thank-you redirect, mobile optimization. Pages load quickly and convert reasonably well for basic lead capture.

For complex funnels with appointment scheduling integration, you'll need to embed third-party widgets or use a dedicated [landing page platform](/reviews/landing-page-builders). AWeber's pages work best for simple email capture rather than full booking flows.

<h3>Segmentation and Tagging</h3>

List segmentation determines email marketing ROI. AWeber offers tag-based segmentation that works well for med spa use cases.

We created segments for:
- Service interest (injectables, body contouring, skincare)
- Client value tier (VIP, regular, prospect)
- Engagement level (active, dormant, at-risk)
- Geographic location (useful for multi-location practices)

The platform supports up to 1,000 tags per subscriber. Segments update in real-time, so your "opened email in last 30 days" segment always reflects current behavior.

<h3>AI Writing Assistant</h3>

AWeber's AI content generator produces subject lines and email copy. We tested it extensively for med spa content.

Results were mixed. The AI generates grammatically correct, professional copy. But it lacks aesthetic industry nuance. We prompted it for "Botox promotional email" and received generic content that could apply to any service business. You'll need to edit heavily to match your brand voice and include procedure-specific details.

The AI works better for structural tasks: generating subject line variations for A/B testing, creating basic newsletter frameworks, drafting re-engagement sequences. Don't expect it to replace a copywriter who understands aesthetic medicine.

<h3>Reporting and Analytics</h3>

AWeber provides standard email metrics: open rates, click rates, unsubscribes, bounces. The dashboard displays trends over time and compares campaign performance.

Advanced analytics include:
- Revenue tracking (when integrated with e-commerce)
- Geographic open data with maps
- Device and email client breakdown
- Automation performance by step

We found the reporting adequate but not exceptional. If you need detailed attribution showing which email campaigns drive bookings, you'll want to integrate AWeber with your [CRM system](/reviews/crm-software) or use UTM tracking with Google Analytics.

<div class="callout-blue">
<strong>💡 Pro Tip:</strong> Create a custom UTM structure for all AWeber campaigns (utm_source=aweber&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=[campaign-name]). This lets you track email-driven appointments in Google Analytics even without direct integration.
</div>

