<h2 id="who-its-for">👥 Who Should Use AWeber?</h2>

<strong>AWeber works best for:</strong>

<ul>
<li><strong>Solo practitioners and small med spas</strong> with under 5,000 subscribers who need straightforward email campaigns without complex automation</li>
<li><strong>Practices prioritizing deliverability</strong> over advanced features—your emails will reach inboxes</li>
<li><strong>Budget-conscious operators</strong> who want professional email marketing for under $100/month</li>
<li><strong>Teams without dedicated marketing staff</strong> who need a platform anyone can learn quickly</li>
<li><strong>Practices already using separate SMS tools</strong> like [Twilio or Podium](/reviews/sms-marketing) and only need email functionality</li>
</ul>

<strong>Consider alternatives if:</strong>

<ul>
<li>You need integrated SMS + email marketing in one platform</li>
<li>Your practice requires deep integration with aesthetic practice management software</li>
<li>You want sophisticated revenue attribution and e-commerce tracking</li>
<li>You're running a multi-location practice needing advanced segmentation and permissions</li>
</ul>

For practices with complex marketing needs, platforms like Klaviyo (better e-commerce features) or Mailchimp (more integrations) might justify their higher costs.

